# Combinational equivalence check: the ivy_to_rtl output for the module-based
# cache CPU (5stage_gen_cache_cpu_ref.il, "gold") against the hand-written
# SystemVerilog golden model (cpu_gen_golden.sv, "gate"). Run from
# doc/examples/hardware after
#   ivy_to_rtl 5stage_gen_cache_cpu_ref.ivy
# with:
#   yosys cpu_gen_equiv.ys
#
# The design is deeply hierarchical: cpu instantiates the branch predictor `bp`
# and the reusable idcache module `idc`, and idc instantiates main_mem/ic/dc.
# Both sides use the SAME instance names (idc, bp, main_mem, ic, dc), so after
# flattening the register/memory names (e.g. idc.main_mem.real_mem, idc.dc.dcache,
# idc.ic.icache, bp.bht, rf) line up and equiv_make pairs them. equiv_induct then
# proves by one-step induction that from any equal state the two compute the same
# next state for every register and memory. rst is tied to 0 (normal operation).

read_rtlil 5stage_gen_cache_cpu_ref.il
rename cpu gold
read_verilog -sv cpu_gen_golden.sv
rename cpu gate
proc

flatten gold
flatten gate

select gold
connect -set rst 1'b0
select gate
connect -set rst 1'b0
select -clear

memory_map

equiv_make gold gate equiv
hierarchy -top equiv
equiv_induct equiv
equiv_status -assert
